# 🐧 Linux Revision

## systemctl status

Command:

```bash
systemctl status ssh
```

Purpose:

Checks whether a service is:

- Running
- Stopped
- Failed

Useful when troubleshooting Linux services.

---

## journalctl -u ssh

Command:

```bash
journalctl -u ssh
```

Purpose:

Displays logs related to the SSH service.

Useful for checking:

- Login attempts
- Authentication failures
- SSH errors
- Service start and stop events

---

# 🌐 Networking Theory

# IP Address

An IP address is a logical address assigned to a device for communication on a network.

Characteristics:

- Layer 3 (Network Layer)
- Can change
- Used for routing data between networks

Example:

```text
192.168.1.100
```

---

# MAC Address

A MAC (Media Access Control) address is the physical hardware address of a network interface.

Characteristics:

- Layer 2 (Data Link Layer)
- Usually permanent
- Used for communication within a local network

Example:

```text
00:1A:2B:3C:4D:5E
```

---

# Difference Between IP Address and MAC Address

| IP Address | MAC Address |
|------------|-------------|
| Logical Address | Physical Address |
| Layer 3 | Layer 2 |
| Can change | Usually permanent |
| Used for routing | Used for local communication |

